  "title": "Carousel with any number of slides, desktop: 7 of 3 and 23 in a row never go back across the seam; 23 in a 12 + 11 grid wrap by columns without a rewind; the filling is out of the accessibility tree",
  "description": "Infinite estrategia-web/carousel with ANY number of slides (plugin 1.4.3) on /prueba-carrusel-impar/: (1) 7 slides with 3 in view (a full turn and beyond with «next», back across the seam with «previous», Home, End, → on the last) and 23 with 4.5 in view (End, then across the seam three times), never going back in any frame; (2) 23 cards in a two-row grid of 12 columns (Lavandería's clients strip: the bottom row has 11): «next» from the last column across the seam three times without going back (the rewind of 1.4.2: scrollLeft 2343 → 1), no card changes row or leaves its column, ← on the first column leads to the last moving left; (3) whatever the carousel adds to fill the grid is aria-hidden, inert, without ids or anything focusable. Every wait is a FACT (__settled: the slide at the edge, still for three frames); the frames are recorded by probes.js. Read by browser-carousel-any-count. It was ./any-count.mjs (sections 1-3), run by carousel.test.mjs (level 3), until 29-10-2026.",
